---
import Layout from '../layout/layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy — Snipy">
	<Nav />
	<main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-16 pt-32">
		<h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy policy</h1>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-semibold">Controller</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-muted">
			The controller under the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP) is the provider named in the <a href="/impressum" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">Impressum</a>.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-semibold">This website</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-muted">
			This site does not use cookies, analytics, tracking, advertising or contact forms. Fonts are served from this
			site itself, not from third parties.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-semibold">Hosting and server logs</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-muted">
			The site is hosted by Vercel Inc., 440 N Barranca Ave #4133, Covina, CA 91723, USA, so your data is
			processed in the USA and other countries where Vercel operates. When you open a page, the server processes
			your IP address, the time of the request, the requested file and the browser's user agent. This is
			technically necessary to deliver the site and keep it secure (legitimate interest). Vercel handles this data
			under its own <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">privacy policy</a>.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-semibold">Download via GitHub</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-muted">
			The Download buttons link to GitHub (GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco, CA 94107,
			USA). If you click one, you leave this site and GitHub processes your data under its own
			<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">privacy statement</a>.
			Nothing is sent to GitHub until you click.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-semibold">The Snipy app</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-muted">
			Snipy works entirely on your device. It copies the text you select to your local clipboard and does not
			send it, or any other data, over the network. The app has no telemetry, accounts or analytics.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-semibold">Your rights</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-muted">
			Under the FADP you can ask what data is held about you, and have it corrected or deleted. You can also
			complain to the Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner (FDPIC). If you visit from the EU,
			the rights under the GDPR apply as well. Contact: see the Impressum.
		</p>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>
